      "p_a_canonical": 0.26094685082901203,
      "prose": {
        "text": "Keep the five-day week.\n\nOne reason is that the data shows a 33% shortfall in revenue per employee after two years, indicating that the intensity of work did not fully compensate for the 20% reduction in hours.",
        "tokens": 46,
        "seconds": 1.8204244939997807,
        "finish": "eos"
      },
      "prose_canonical": "B",
      "prose_letter_slot": null
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "discount": false,
      "printed_order": 2,
      "mass": 0.9971483118612822,
      "p_a_slot": 0.05415190511320767,
      "p_a_canonical": 0.9458480948867923,
      "prose": {
        "text": "Move to a four-day week.\n\nOne reason is that the initial productivity gain from eliminating redundant meetings can be sustained for a short period, but it is not a long-term solution. The study found that the early gain was a one-off, and the billable-hour recovery was only 71% after two years, indicating that the intensity of work had to be increased to compensate for the reduced hours, but not fully.",
        "tokens": 85,
        "seconds": 3.2670660559997486,
        "finish": "eos"
      },
      "prose_canonical": "A",
      "prose_letter_slot": null
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "discount": true,
      "printed_order": 1,
      "mass": 0.9631479011116681,
      "p_a_slot": 0.3166393206141814,
      "p_a_canonical": 0.3166393206141814,
      "prose": {
        "text": "I choose: Keep the five-day week.\n\nOne reason is that a four-day week may lead to reduced hours for clients, which could negatively impact the firm's revenue and competitiveness.",
        "tokens": 37,
        "seconds": 1.4631846420006696,
        "finish": "eos"
      },
      "prose_canonical": "B",
      "prose_letter_slot": null
    },
    {
